WEBVTT

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:04.400
Yoshida-san.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.780
Please let me get a job.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.240
Sure.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.050
I-It's okay?

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.590
Did you have to get on your knees to ask?

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:20.480
W-Well, we'd agreed I'd do the chores.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.390
You're doing more than enough.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.250
And staying in this room all day 
can't be good for you, mentally.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.250
I'd feel better if you got a job, really.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.090
Really?

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.450
I guess, yeah.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.010
Anyway, got any place in mind?

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:40.090
Yeah, the convenience store near here.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.930
Convenience store, huh?

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.080
There might be kids your age there.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.150
Yeah.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.860
If you're lucky, you'll make some friends.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.030
Yeah!

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.890
You didn't graduate high school? Really?

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:26.490
That's insane!

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.750
Is it...?

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.710
You're totally awesome, Sayu-chaso!

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:33.920
"Part-Time Job"

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.640
Sayu-chaso?

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.090
So, when they want to pay with credit,

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:39.290
you press this button and
run the card through here, 'kay?

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.430
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.850
And why are you so polite?

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.650
That's hilarious. We're the same age!

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:50.310
But you're my superior at this job, Yuuki-san.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.750
Who cares?

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.360
And call me "Asami."

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:58.570
Y-Yes, understood... I mean, got it!

00:02:59.080 --> 00:02:59.870
Good.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.350
Laters.

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:03.530
Goodnight!

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.240
So, where do you live, Sayu-chaso?

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.000
About five minutes from here.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.270
Same as me.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:16.250
Maybe we live really close. That's hilarious!

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.260
Is that funny...?

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.420
Okay, let me come to your place soon.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:24.600
I don't know.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.240
I'm not sure the person I'm living with 
would be okay with it.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.230
The person you're living with?

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.990
The way you said that 
sounds like they're not family.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.520
Living with your boyfriend?

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.400
No, he's not my boyfriend.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.940
It's a guy, like a brother, 
who's been helping me out.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.600
Like a brother. So not a brother.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.200
That's kind of bad, right?

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:56.520
Well, I'm going to your place anyway. 
I need to see what kind of guy he is.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.460
Today's fine, right?

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:10.890
<b>My senpai at my job is coming over.
Sorry, I couldn't refuse.
I think she'll be here until you get home.
Oh, it's a girl.
I explained that you're like a big brother.</b>

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.650
<i>Like a big brother, huh?</i>

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.620
<i>Roger...</i>

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.280
Sayu-chan?

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.440
Don't peek at my phone!

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.530
You've got a narrow field 
of vision, Yoshida-san.

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.240
Oh, you told Mishima-chan?

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.690
It just kind of slipped out.

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:31.020
Slipped out, eh?

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:34.370
So Hashimoto-senpai knew?

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.580
Why didn't you tell me?

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.050
Why do I have to tell you?

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:45.610
A new employee and her supervisor
are bound by threads of fate!

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.180
I don't think it's right to hide things.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.020
<i>Coming!</i>

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:03.630
Welcome back—

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.360
Yikes! He's an old dude!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.990
But he may be kind of hot.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.540
But he's got the aura of an older dude!

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:12.580
What a waste!

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:15.100
Oh, I'm Asami.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:18.290
Just call me Asami, 
and don't worry about it, okay?

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.550
O-Okay.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:23.880
Like, why the heck is a girl living
with a guy who's not her boyfriend?

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.610
And there's like no room in this apartment.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:27.260
I was really worried.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.030
But he seems like a decent guy. 
I'm relieved.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.610
Okay, okay.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:34.990
I see.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:38.010
So you used to play together 
when you were young?

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:40.700
Yeah, I guess. Kinda.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:44.230
But you two are nine years apart, 
right, Yoshida-cchi?

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:48.700
When Sayu-chaso just got to elementary school, 
you were in high school.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:52.100
It's a mystery how you'd play together.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:58.490
Well, it was more like 
he was looking after me.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:00.890
My parents weren't home a lot.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:02.390
Right, Yoshida-san?

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.590
Y-Yeah, that's right.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.720
By the way, you don't cook, Yoshida-cchi?

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.530
Not really.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:16.030
Only when I feel like it on the weekends.

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:18.970
So it's Sayu-chaso's job.

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:21.690
She does all the chores.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.460
How much good karma 
do you have from your last life,

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:29.270
to have a cute girl like her 
looking after you?

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:32.880
I don't think I did anything special.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.200
I just—

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:36.910
Just?

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:43.180
Yoshida-san, it's almost done. 
So get the rice in the bowls.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:44.810
Uh, sure!

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:53.610
Wow, you can really cook!

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.010
You're like the ideal woman!

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.810
Thanks.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:07:00.230
You're staying for dinner uninvited, huh?

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:05.230
I think I'm just barely O.K. Corral 
with eating from the same plate as you.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:08.740
"O.K. Corral"? What era is that from?

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:17.370
Okay, let's eat.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.120
It's great!

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:24.730
What is this?

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:27.240
You get to eat this every day, Yoshida-cchi?

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.200
You're the luckiest guy on Earth!

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.220
Holy shit!

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:36.180
Anyway, your place is super-tiny.

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:40.250
There'll be more room when you leave.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:41.760
I'm resting now.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.870
You just ate too much.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.700
Don't be so mean, soul mate.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:47.520
I'm not your soul mate!

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.510
You're good friends now, huh?

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:51.640
How?

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:55.500
Anyway, I'll be heading home.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:58.450
Walk me back, Yoshida-cchi?

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:00.660
Why?

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:05.380
It's not every day you get a chance 
to escort a pretty girl like me.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.280
Oh, fine.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:08.250
Jeez.

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.330
I'll go, too.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.910
You stay here.

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:15.370
It's a man's job to be an escort.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:17.630
Let's go, and don't get any weird ideas.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.560
Not in a million years.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:21.830
See you later, Sayu-chaso.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:26.830
Okay, let's hurry, Yoshida-cchi!

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:28.520
Wait!

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:33.060
By the way, Yoshida-cchi.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.950
What's the deal with you and Sayu-chaso?

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.780
I told you. We're childhood—

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:44.140
You're the worst liar in the world.

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:47.460
It's obvious you're making it all up.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:53.230
Your gaze was bouncing around so much 
when you were talking about your past

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:55.680
that I thought it was an acrobatics competition.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:00.600
You can tell me the truth, you know.

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.590
Sayu and I...

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:32.700
What she said is true, to her.

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:38.550
If she sees me as a big brother,

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:42.180
there's no need for anybody else 
to say otherwise.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:47.270
In other words, just forget it, huh?

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:52.280
That's the same as admitting you were lying.

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:55.610
I'm not persuasive enough 
to come up with new lies to hide the ones

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.050
you've already seen through.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:58.740
And...

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:03.450
I think it's not right for me 
to talk about things she wants to hide.

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:10.890
You're a surprisingly good guy, Yoshida-cchi.

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:13.880
Sayu-chaso was really lucky.

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:19.800
You can choose who you get involved with, 
but you can't choose who you meet.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:26.770
So I think you're really lucky 
when you meet a good person.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.500
I'll head home the rest of the way myself.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:34.000
What about my chance to escort 
a pretty girl like you?

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:36.530
You'll get another one.

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:38.240
And...

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.140
I don't want you seeing where I live.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.360
I see.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.660
Well, be careful on your way home.

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:47.500
I know I'm late saying this, 
but sorry for barging in today.

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:52.830
It's fine. It didn't bother me that much, 
except for how cramped the place got.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:55.550
I really like that place, though.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.560
Including how cramped it is.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:00.670
Then come back sometime.

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:01.930
Really?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.890
Be Sayu's friend.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:10.560
You're like her dad! You're hilarious!

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:12.960
I'm like a big brother.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:14.800
Her guardian, yeah.

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:18.520
So here's some advice for her guardian.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:24.200
Sayu-chaso's really good 
at using different smiles.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.640
So be careful.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:42.140
It's done.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:52.350
<b>Work's over and I'm heading home</b>

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:53.480
Yoshida-kun.

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:55.610
Gotou-san?

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:57.420
You done for the day?

00:11:58.310 --> 00:11:59.650
I-I guess.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:03.860
I see. Then would you come with me?

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:30.490
Sayu-chaso's really good 
at using different smiles.

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:31.960
So be careful.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:36.570
<i>But what am I supposed to do, exactly?</i>

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:43.400
I knew it. Meat tastes better
when <i>you</i> cook it.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:46.110
I'm just better at not overcooking it.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.070
So, what is it today?

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:49.740
"What is it"?

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:52.740
You wanted something, right?

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:56.440
You brought me out here.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.710
The last time we met like this,

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:03.920
you said there was nothing going on 
between you and Mishima-san, right?

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:06.720
That again?

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:10.200
But when I see you, you look so close.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:15.680
And I heard you actually turned down 
a business trip for the first time.

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:16.900
Well...

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.640
No. I'm not blaming you.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:27.270
But I thought there must be some reason.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:33.640
And you never used to play 
with your phone during work,

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:35.760
but now you're looking at it all the time.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:39.320
I'm wondering if you're messaging someone.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:40.790
I see.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:44.790
And... Well?

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.010
Well...

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:51.760
First, can I ask something?

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:53.240
What?

00:13:54.230 --> 00:14:00.280
I asked you before, 
but why do you care so much about what I do?

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:05.940
If you don't answer me, I won't answer you.

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:08.870
That's true.

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:12.970
I focus on you more than other people.

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:14.450
That's true.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:17.350
Um...

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:20.910
I don't want you to be surprised.

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:23.670
No, I'm sure you will.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:25.130
Huh?

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.400
I...

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:30.880
It's because...

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:38.310
It's because I like you!

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:44.900
Okay, it's done!

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:51.760
Nice job, if I do say so myself.

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:54.040
Time to tell Yoshida-san!

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:06.050
<b>Sorry, Gotou-san asked to go out for dinner. 
I won't be home for supper tonight.</b>

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:14.230
"Roger. Have fun."

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:21.800
And it tastes so good, too.

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:28.870
Y-You're kidding, right?

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:31.950
I'm not.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.870
But you said you had a boyfriend! 
One you'd been dating for five years!

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:42.980
Oh, that...

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:44.500
That was a lie.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.760
What do you mean?

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:53.780
I-I'm sorry.

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:57.720
My intuition's pretty good, you see.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:15:59.280
Your intuition?

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:03.820
Yeah. When you told me you liked me, 
I was really happy.

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:06.660
I wanted to jump for joy, actually.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:11.800
But I thought that it wasn't the time.

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:14.010
The time?

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:15.030
Right.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:22.160
Even if I agreed then, it wouldn't go well.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:25.660
And that was your intuition?

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:27.830
And so I just kind of...

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:31.740
You kind of said you had a boyfriend.

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:35.140
I don't believe you.

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:41.360
It doesn't seem you like me at all.

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:44.100
That's not true! I always have.

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:48.110
This is actually just your way 
of making fun of me, right?

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.200
Of course not!

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:52.150
What would it take to make you believe me?

00:16:59.160 --> 00:16:59.780
Then...

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:02.680
Could you sleep with me?

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:14.740
Um...

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:19.540
I was kidding.

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:31.160
I-I'm a virgin.

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:32.320
Is that okay?

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:36.760
Are you okay?

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:43.080
Do you not like virgins?

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:47.180
I'm really sorry for saying
something so stupid!

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:48.410
Forget it!

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.220
But you shouldn't lie to me!

00:17:52.220 --> 00:17:53.720
About being a virgin—

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:57.080
But... it's not my fault!

00:17:57.480 --> 00:17:59.980
I never had a chance.

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:03.850
Then you're really—

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:05.850
I really do like you!

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:11.820
So if you want...

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.780
A-And if that happened...

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:18.740
Really, it was a joke.

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:20.340
A joke?

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:23.700
You mean you were lying?

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:24.730
No.

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:26.660
Well...

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.070
I'll wait.

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:44.010
Wait?

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:49.280
But I'm never going to ask you out again.

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:52.520
When the time comes, you ask me to date you.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:58.080
You never come out and
say anything yourself, anyway.

00:18:58.080 --> 00:18:59.740
I don't mean to.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.700
And that's what makes it even worse.

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:05.180
You don't need to get mad.

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:08.240
Do you really even like me, Yoshida-kun?

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:09.770
I do!

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:12.010
And that's why it's so frustrating.

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:21.430
It hurts when the person you like 
makes a mess of your life.

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:24.760
If you really like me...

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:28.340
It's not fair unless you end where I am.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.550
All right.

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:38.390
I don't know when, 
but someday I'll ask you to date me.

00:19:41.190 --> 00:19:42.810
Please do.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:45.750
Now then...

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:48.780
I've given you my answer.

00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:51.000
Now it's your turn.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.620
Oh.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:57.170
Let's eat.

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:03.340
It's good, but...

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:06.800
Not as good as it should be.

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:15.640
I thought I was used to it, 
but being alone feels lonely again.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:18.250
Again?

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.030
Sayu-chan!

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:49.550
<i>If Yoshida-san had come home...</i>

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:55.190
<i>I'm blaming it on someone else again.</i>

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:57.780
<i>Really, nothing's changed.</i>

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:14.090
<i>Taking her with him?</i>

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:16.420
<i>Here?</i>

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:19.510
<i>Gotou-san?</i>

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.420
<i>I see.</i>

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:41.020
<i>I'm going to be abandoned again.</i>

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:55.410
<b>Sorry, this is really sudden, 
but I'm bringing Gotou-san home.</b>

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:56.210
<b>OK! I'll stay somewhere else!</b>

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:56.210
<b>No, that's not it. She wants to meet you.</b>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:34.970
"Reality"

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>So yeah...</b>

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>See you next week!</b>
